From 8fb6a0b269c4cb027870baa6a9780deceb9af25e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:42:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 26/26] experiment: nx2:gpu handlers queue GPU work only after
 releasing the region lock (Tegra::DeferGpuQueue)

Handlers 102, 213, 214 and 216 held m_region_mutex while the registry's listeners and their own
RunInOrder/SignalAfterGpu calls pushed onto the GPU thread's queue, which blocks while the queue is
full; the GPU's back thread takes m_region_mutex to back sparse blocks on write (BackSparseWrite).
A DeferGpuQueue opened before the lock holds those pushes and makes them, in order, after it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/core/hle/service/nx2_gsv.h |  5 ++++
 src/video_core/gpu.cpp         | 45 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 src/video_core/gpu.h           | 14 +++++++++++
 3 files changed, 58 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/core/hle/service/nx2_gsv.h b/src/core/hle/service/nx2_gsv.h
